                        ],
                        "form": "zélés"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "687041e5-9dec-4a3b-8e46-bcb64ca22cfe",
                        "entry_id": "44d45ea7-8176-3778-96a4-5b55713c0cab",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "zélée"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8704399a-738f-4d76-ac1a-a5bb44db4375",
                        "entry_id": "44d45ea7-8176-3778-96a4-5b55713c0cab",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "zélées"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "629b270f-3048-3917-9608-f6887df5648c",
                        "entry_id": "44d45ea7-8176-3778-96a4-5b55713c0cab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a du zèle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04349a5e-58c7-432d-b22a-c0ba7aee638f",
                                "sense_id": "629b270f-3048-3917-9608-f6887df5648c",
                                "text": "Que la Bretagne, considérée dans son ensemble, soit encore aujourd'hui, une province de zélée pratique religieuse, voilà, je crois, un point qui ne sera contesté sérieusement par personne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a1fead1-6e0f-4d54-9c91-ac2ffd96179d",
                                "sense_id": "629b270f-3048-3917-9608-f6887df5648c",
                                "text": "— Et vous dites qu'il est à la Bastille ?\n — Oui, sire. Pour s'être montré trop zélé à votre défense."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "81af8d07-469e-4163-8cd9-31ac92a9ba53",
                        "source_entry_id": "44d45ea7-8176-3778-96a4-5b55713c0cab",
                        "source_sense_id": "629b270f-3048-3917-9608-f6887df5648c",
                        "target_lang_word": "eifrig",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eifrig",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9c693a6-80b9-3807-8289-32793df7fc1a",
                                        "entry_id": "12ec2d71-8880-37ec-b001-a3ba14c61557",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "großen persönlichen Einsatz bei der Arbeit an einer Sache aufweisend"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e90d1f51-5382-40c6-b0dc-88fde4334b23",
                                                "sense_id": "d9c693a6-80b9-3807-8289-32793df7fc1a",
                                                "text": "Er war schon immer ein eifriger Schüler mit guten Erfolgen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc797c59-c295-4aef-a22e-04e83f3db33c",
                                                "sense_id": "d9c693a6-80b9-3807-8289-32793df7fc1a",
                                                "text": "„Während die Munitionsfabriken längst eifrig produzieren und auch ein Mangel an Nahrung vorerst nicht zu befürchten steht, schenkt man im Kriegsministerium den essenziellen ökonomischen Fragen keinerlei Beachtung.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14d84852-f9c9-4447-8e4f-102582734fee",
                        "source_entry_id": "44d45ea7-8176-3778-96a4-5b55713c0cab",
                        "source_sense_id": "629b270f-3048-3917-9608-f6887df5648c",
                        "target_lang_word": "zealous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "zealous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                        "entry_id": "eb8de8af-46ce-3e49-b418-07e01873d81a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Full of zeal; ardent, fervent; exhibiting enthusiasm or strong passion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf5b6883-f9d1-42b7-a62d-6387a1b1eef3",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "They neuer paſſe for the procuring of Gods honor, neither regard they how much they be bound vnto him. But euery man in the meane ſeaſon followes his owne likings. One burnes in couetouſneſſe, and another in vaine glorie, ſeeking to be aduaunced to authoritie and honour, and to bee taken to be I wote not what. Thus ye ſee at what point they bee, which will needes be taken to bee greateſt and zealouſeſt Chriſtians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f148786-c6a2-454e-9c0e-b6ec6faa78bf",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "I had almoſt forgotten to acquaint your honor, that one major Alford (who was in mr. Love's conſpiracy) was of the graund inqueſt at Saliſbury, and was very zealous in his highneſſe ſervice here, and his good affection and wiſe carriage here, did much advantage the buſſineſe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5cfe154-432f-42c3-b646-84655e1b56a7",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "[S]orting them into ſeveral congregations of a moderat number, out of the ableſt and zealouſeſt among them to create elders, who, exerciſing and requiring from themſelves what they have learnd (for no learning is retaind without conſtant exerciſe and methodical repetition) may reach and govern the reſt: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1caaa410-2847-4341-84e7-205d28cd293f",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Johnſon was truly zealous for the ſucceſs of \"The Adventurer;\" and very ſoon after his engaging in it, he wrote the following letter […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbc1815e-01f4-4df2-9147-022b74b93ddb",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Doubtless many will exclaim against the Roman Catholic Church for this; but the simple truth is that Protestantism was no less zealous against the new scientific doctrine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db4fd36e-7b4e-4734-a4aa-46eae44c5c78",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Newt Gingrich […] left Congress in 1998, following GOP midterm-election losses that many blamed on his zealous pursuit of Bill Clinton's impeachment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbf80a7e-34b6-4304-89f4-7d93dc37bfd2",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Britain’s police are especially zealous. Officers spend thousands of hours sifting through potentially offensive posts and arrest 30 people a day. Among those collared were a man who ranted about immigration on Facebook and a couple who criticised their daughter’s primary school."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
